    2. Choose two distinct non-black colors color_A (ring) and color_B (center).
    3. Place the 3x3 frame at a random valid position (center r in [1,H-2], c in [1,W-2]).
    4. Scatter 0-12 extra color_A pixels and 7-12 extra color_B pixels on empty (black) cells.
    5. Validate no accidental second 3x3 frame exists; if one does, remove/relocate the offending pixel.
    6. Output is [[color_B]].
